{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:38:01Z","created_by_operation":"op_146197f74bbb419c80f9b21a19f79497","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_0bc4802f7de30dd2f1cdd9662f3ed9ad003e6045e5b7e2ae88212abf3bb15ed4","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"betterforall/self-improving-agents@5f7823732d87 snapshot 2ffba66f8aa5de4e","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_2b9e3b556403f601a8d91d640654b9ab4ff3109f729f1d7f02ab9fa32a450f8d","slc_d97213a8fa0c595e02e2f80f65ec59c9ff8cb9a7e9d57d103e7a106bd6876f8d"],"source_ids":["src_f718246686d85a4fa768db72f9e241cd"],"text":"Level 2 (feedback-loop/) adds a reviewer agent that returns structured feedback (issue type, severity, fix suggestion, confidence, detected pattern) explaining why a solution failed.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:38:01Z","updated_by_operation":"op_146197f74bbb419c80f9b21a19f79497"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:38:01Z","created_by_operation":"op_146197f74bbb419c80f9b21a19f79497","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_19a0eee0ba107a0ddb18d99ad3f27112b746e4c3976f1ca7935d4aba9006bc96","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"betterforall/self-improving-agents@5f7823732d87 snapshot 2ffba66f8aa5de4e","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_34ea7813252a53e6091dbe4c935798503ab1a6fa752479773fe2b26c62310912","slc_7e5807a0ba4321302ccee86a412348609a0ac3f4634755e1deafe50ff84e0ee6"],"source_ids":["src_f718246686d85a4fa768db72f9e241cd"],"text":"Each level is run via a run.py entry point (e.g. python autoresearch/run.py) with a --task flag selecting tasks such as snake, support, or email_validation.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:38:01Z","updated_by_operation":"op_146197f74bbb419c80f9b21a19f79497"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:38:01Z","created_by_operation":"op_146197f74bbb419c80f9b21a19f79497","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_1df0d851293d033a7673e0ce3e0f918a93633f344ead8594917281c1655e7ac7","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"betterforall/self-improving-agents@5f7823732d87 snapshot 2ffba66f8aa5de4e","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_19c67d983cf5238cbb844321af0838d99a9ee1062e8d5bc53639535baca7f409","slc_1eae84115f6d6f704268e032178f12b1abd6e6ce8ba99f97e9286c701766071d","slc_c3fc43a078d584587f7d429f42a56a39ec6c3a0b010020489e04854ed8fe9424"],"source_ids":["src_f718246686d85a4fa768db72f9e241cd"],"text":"run_all.py runs experiments across all levels and generates comparison analysis, supporting --levels/--tasks filters and a --fresh flag to ignore previous results; analyze_results.py performs cross-level comparison after experiments are done.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:38:01Z","updated_by_operation":"op_146197f74bbb419c80f9b21a19f79497"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:38:01Z","created_by_operation":"op_146197f74bbb419c80f9b21a19f79497","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_3463f9d610c8dc6a766bad608c5e5a04d9fb7385a2b98eb27059e7a33a4d5930","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=evaluation","setting":"betterforall/self-improving-agents@5f7823732d87 snapshot 2ffba66f8aa5de4e","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_2d2c36deb53401f493bc7ec2541e39b569560520bab08ca589d6b663efafaeef","slc_3d12ce640ae72cc3261b32eb2fcbfbb3d8f8b5b56fb762a7bba5b6c36eb0ae43","slc_5661709aa3a954b3da4c6b6597630e2f692f9eddd56ce52bc0f63c34707dbc24"],"source_ids":["src_f87ec2c135f0505ab547d3c3b21bc3e1"],"text":"Cross-validation shows Levels 1-3 scored 90-100% on email_validation's original 20 tests but dropped to 62-66% on the expanded 50-case adversarial suite, while Arena levels held at 70% on the combined suite.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:38:01Z","updated_by_operation":"op_146197f74bbb419c80f9b21a19f79497"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:38:01Z","created_by_operation":"op_146197f74bbb419c80f9b21a19f79497","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_3635219370eec55e0ecfdf9529f5a9c497b299772a7a475768c7e546ca20e66d","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"betterforall/self-improving-agents@5f7823732d87 snapshot 2ffba66f8aa5de4e","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_3b58f0305d6868bfd0508cef936d4e87fe008dfaabc9579a35e8977b86013493","slc_466c151705bc03948f5f5658891fc0c24d74487ac1a50170dbf96b7d51d4c013"],"source_ids":["src_f718246686d85a4fa768db72f9e241cd"],"text":"HyperAgent rewrites are validated by a three-stage crash recovery: compile check, import check, and signature check; invalid rewrites revert to the last valid generation.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:38:01Z","updated_by_operation":"op_146197f74bbb419c80f9b21a19f79497"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:38:01Z","created_by_operation":"op_146197f74bbb419c80f9b21a19f79497","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_37d669749a1aa9d659d22f1371bb6089d098315e785f42762f5910572a1b24f8","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=dependencies","setting":"betterforall/self-improving-agents@5f7823732d87 snapshot 2ffba66f8aa5de4e","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_21caa59eef4a7f42bd6fb7773d045cc631f6057946192634687241a34ab5eb06","slc_292cc368846724ecfca5556598c898239c22f5b9af0054f7c275314d8eec2c2f","slc_59cbbc7e81e837feeb2b1067e228831b32d04be1543e38a4c912c7921f1c51e7"],"source_ids":["src_f718246686d85a4fa768db72f9e241cd"],"text":"Setup requires installing requirements.txt via pip and creating a .env file in the repo root containing a GEMINI_API_KEY obtained from Google AI Studio.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:38:01Z","updated_by_operation":"op_146197f74bbb419c80f9b21a19f79497"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:38:01Z","created_by_operation":"op_146197f74bbb419c80f9b21a19f79497","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_435cbe12a8f0f615010d13bb0e01d8342346e3d50f66b48033a15e25253f3544","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"betterforall/self-improving-agents@5f7823732d87 snapshot 2ffba66f8aa5de4e","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_2ae0e3ea8b92b3a0ad72e5572a3db02f072d0ecc07492ec36a4a12cfdcac5e60"],"source_ids":["src_f718246686d85a4fa768db72f9e241cd"],"text":"HyperAgent is a simplification of Meta's HyperAgents (DGM-H): it uses folder-based versioning instead of Docker containers.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:38:01Z","updated_by_operation":"op_146197f74bbb419c80f9b21a19f79497"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:38:01Z","created_by_operation":"op_146197f74bbb419c80f9b21a19f79497","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_450b80a4589363c19dd28eee16b4c76a2f440bdb97fc4839cbc23a350792ed18","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"betterforall/self-improving-agents@5f7823732d87 snapshot 2ffba66f8aa5de4e","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_025ec169614a483685b676a23f0bcd83cacf2668505381e36c21cad049c9c685","slc_e14fc64e643616221c8e6f8d65406e43d9d056aa0c5383b72c9f9cd9a50afbeb"],"source_ids":["src_f718246686d85a4fa768db72f9e241cd"],"text":"Level 4a (Arena Single) pits one code agent against one test agent in adversarial co-evolution without tournament or population dynamics; 4b adds tournament selection where the worst agents are replaced by mutated winners.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:38:01Z","updated_by_operation":"op_146197f74bbb419c80f9b21a19f79497"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:38:01Z","created_by_operation":"op_146197f74bbb419c80f9b21a19f79497","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_51e11ff704badfb13491898d069d20db68b7748c442be796ec5e95428f9bb1f5","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"betterforall/self-improving-agents@5f7823732d87 snapshot 2ffba66f8aa5de4e","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_b1bd3f28b98995510f0a028d74d97bfb616d2ff0119512945934ea421722c113","slc_cebdccddf823da8a6663b817df34c407149e1def258139649ea61f35a56df0da"],"source_ids":["src_f718246686d85a4fa768db72f9e241cd"],"text":"Level 2 uses asymmetric information: the worker gets a small prompt with just the code, while the reviewer sees full history and prior feedback to spot cross-iteration patterns.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:38:01Z","updated_by_operation":"op_146197f74bbb419c80f9b21a19f79497"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:38:01Z","created_by_operation":"op_146197f74bbb419c80f9b21a19f79497","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_546ec871b016f409478943efd740748638af2072056e095487e4d61ed4559723","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"betterforall/self-improving-agents@5f7823732d87 snapshot 2ffba66f8aa5de4e","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_3f591a9fdb1639941d6d79e6683c0bb0d620076a22b75115df257e6c887e1558","slc_7bc6740677dd138fce308e46b9985c921ad7a2fa783b43321418ca9b17f2d801","slc_d230f58a0241cc9c092e45704b69f70b4bd4ac1bc703b044978049696ff36482"],"source_ids":["src_f718246686d85a4fa768db72f9e241cd"],"text":"Level 1 (autoresearch/) is a single-agent loop: the LLM proposes code, it is written to a file, benchmarked, kept if better, and repeated; bad proposals revert immediately.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:38:01Z","updated_by_operation":"op_146197f74bbb419c80f9b21a19f79497"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:38:01Z","created_by_operation":"op_146197f74bbb419c80f9b21a19f79497","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_70559fc3ab565d228764941c42db1cffbaba2f0a46ec4681726845199516f74a","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=evaluation","setting":"betterforall/self-improving-agents@5f7823732d87 snapshot 2ffba66f8aa5de4e","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_33a668c6482d1f185546b2ac71bdc2db2191c7c626b2d4fa4e2c1eb10873e0f4","slc_94c12c997734e8293617449bcc45752dcc3f2d8cc3021c7f2d28507d389ce55b"],"source_ids":["src_f87ec2c135f0505ab547d3c3b21bc3e1"],"text":"Experiments used Gemini 2.5 Flash across five levels and three tasks (email_validation, snake, support) in 15 total experiments, with per-level metrics, costs, and token counts reported.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:38:01Z","updated_by_operation":"op_146197f74bbb419c80f9b21a19f79497"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:38:01Z","created_by_operation":"op_146197f74bbb419c80f9b21a19f79497","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_709413796f564831061a919454bea05436e47a82627baf60c852b71846519bfe","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"betterforall/self-improving-agents@5f7823732d87 snapshot 2ffba66f8aa5de4e","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_14f5633d47d89cfb931a37c6ef905348be96e7682d92b0d64beb9d7794fbbeba","slc_589157d4b264c8b9a26ba282b18ae6101bf5ec14d2ef66fed8a022619a188c3d","slc_85e645d47ff45b775313730c92c4fce461786c0409485e20540b10920f8a6f0c","slc_cd714af84c84cc59b89e318cbda2edaabb598b8bb79ef8d6936a7091e11c34b6"],"source_ids":["src_f718246686d85a4fa768db72f9e241cd"],"text":"The framework is task-agnostic: a new task is a folder in tasks/ with config.py (task name, metric, direction, prompt builder), initial_solution.py, and a benchmark.py that prints 'metric_name:value' to stdout.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:38:01Z","updated_by_operation":"op_146197f74bbb419c80f9b21a19f79497"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:38:01Z","created_by_operation":"op_146197f74bbb419c80f9b21a19f79497","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_9330320c5a646097cdfdf3a2af2509ded50ce4fea9819d67d6d57cf4b7fb9cdf","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=evaluation","setting":"betterforall/self-improving-agents@5f7823732d87 snapshot 2ffba66f8aa5de4e","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_4d7cbc358e599ff3556f3f1ce30c0f3c4efdd99a4410302f5a78858168fe0e79","slc_5f89472715997ca9a6370a46f2783f2c28b9583488b6a48a2feba172a89eea61","slc_73862df3cba0536bb3aabe9050a8a536724f5877b81214f37c3a923adac9e9df"],"source_ids":["src_f87ec2c135f0505ab547d3c3b21bc3e1"],"text":"For support, rubric-based boolean scoring (keyword match plus LLM YES/NO fallback) reduced judge noise from over 30 points to under 7; Feedback Loop scored highest (82.091) on the expanded 19 questions.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:38:01Z","updated_by_operation":"op_146197f74bbb419c80f9b21a19f79497"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:38:01Z","created_by_operation":"op_146197f74bbb419c80f9b21a19f79497","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_b2959b1a14e2b33efbbaeed7e88caecdb96af78e57a504f170a30b79db7e4b87","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=memory-state","setting":"betterforall/self-improving-agents@5f7823732d87 snapshot 2ffba66f8aa5de4e","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_6cf9b3e32532376a8531c0622824048a74db9f8c02b63e284e32fa9ab01fa7d2"],"source_ids":["src_f718246686d85a4fa768db72f9e241cd"],"text":"All levels share tasks/checkpoint.py for resumable checkpointing using sequence-numbered JSON files with atomic writes (write to .tmp then os.replace), keeping only the last three checkpoints.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:38:01Z","updated_by_operation":"op_146197f74bbb419c80f9b21a19f79497"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:38:01Z","created_by_operation":"op_146197f74bbb419c80f9b21a19f79497","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_bcc5ed44ba5fa941733988366c022b83dfc64d30bc8d963ce970b2f3ba2e11f4","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"betterforall/self-improving-agents@5f7823732d87 snapshot 2ffba66f8aa5de4e","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_3355816c7b5b4ffea11a299a3000cb08abf8e881aaa9454625ac6a7100416e21"],"source_ids":["src_f718246686d85a4fa768db72f9e241cd"],"text":"In Arena Loop, code agents are described as mini-HyperAgents that can mutate their own propose() function, so the code-generating code itself evolves.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:38:01Z","updated_by_operation":"op_146197f74bbb419c80f9b21a19f79497"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:38:01Z","created_by_operation":"op_146197f74bbb419c80f9b21a19f79497","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_d6243040169d98da0b1a5c247c38910c14cfafcc6aae1dd1964d5d642b725f36","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=specifications","setting":"betterforall/self-improving-agents@5f7823732d87 snapshot 2ffba66f8aa5de4e","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_01a50f2ed041f4042fca94275b39802d806aca166da43b818b1916654e58c950"],"source_ids":["src_f718246686d85a4fa768db72f9e241cd"],"text":"The project defines four levels of self-improving code agents, each adding one key idea, from a simple improvement loop to an adversarial arena with self-modifying agents.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:38:01Z","updated_by_operation":"op_146197f74bbb419c80f9b21a19f79497"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:38:01Z","created_by_operation":"op_146197f74bbb419c80f9b21a19f79497","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_df7163e766e5e41ca37312726e33c4ac886d4ea4c7f407019df11cf2007853c7","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=relevance","setting":"betterforall/self-improving-agents@5f7823732d87 snapshot 2ffba66f8aa5de4e","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_36bce60cd3f40c3040f2fdb930dd4c119aad2beef90bc3e1b90ca7d8845e2e3b","slc_4855f0dd24c0022814087c9f75181002cc7015eb85dcf8f8a0e9fc260dbb52db","slc_8d16ad15d44dfcf03a3ff0866cb7664fb461bed17e2683e6c4a41c86530a6add"],"source_ids":["src_f718246686d85a4fa768db72f9e241cd"],"text":"The project frames itself as independent research comparing existing self-improving code-agent approaches and proposing new ones, with lineage traced to AlphaGo/RLVR, AutoResearch, HyperAgents, and GAN-style co-evolution.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:38:01Z","updated_by_operation":"op_146197f74bbb419c80f9b21a19f79497"}
